From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 04:30:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 03/15] pcie_fdt: leave plain SMC GPIO output rails to the OS

pcie_prepare_fdt() powers every enabled T8132 port that carries
pwren-gpios and knows a single rail: the radio's REG_ON, the qualified
gP13 pKW4 action (template 0x00800000) that the handoff must apply before
Linux adopts the live link. Any other rail fails preparation, and kboot
then disables the whole controller, radio included. The J604 describes
its SD reader port (pci@2,0) the way the t600x and t602x SD reader ports
are described: pwren-gpios on the SMC GPIO line of the ADT's
pcie-sdreader function-sd_pwr_en, which is pKW4(gP19, 0). With that tree
the J604 lost Wi-Fi and Bluetooth.

Classify a port's rail by type instead. A rail the ADT describes as a
plain SMC GPIO output, where every pKW4 function of that line belongs to
the SMC PMU and has a zero template, is the OS's. pcie-apple drives it
through pwren-gpios before it trains the port, as on every other Apple
SoC and on the T8132 J773g, so the handoff neither powers that port nor
bypasses its DART stream, and logs "pcie: leaving the rail of <port> to
the OS". The endpoint behind the port is not consulted. gP13 keeps its
qualified path and is never left to the OS. A rail the ADT does not
describe, describes with a template, or that is wired active-low, stays
refused, and so does a second port on the qualified action. All rails are
classified before any is powered.

The J604 values come from its ADT: 26B123 template and 27.2 runtime ADT
amfm function-reg_on = pKW4(gP13, 0x00800000), apcie pci-bridge2
pcie-sdreader and pcie-sdreader-helper function-sd_pwr_en =
pKW4(gP19, 0), smc-pmu AAPL,phandle 0x10d. The M4 Pro J614s ADT has the
same sd_pwr_en action, gP19 with template 0.

tests: test_m4_pcie_power_fdt gains an ADT model and test_os_rail_port().
On J713 and J604 trees, and whatever the endpoint is, a plain-output port
is left alone: one gP13 write, one SID16 bypass, pwren-gpios retained.
The test refuses a missing ADT, a line the ADT does not describe, a
template, conflicting functions, another provider, active-low wiring, a
second gP13 port and an out-of-range line. The new test fails against the
previous pcie_fdt.c.

